{"availability":"available","full":"HerringtonDarkholme/hd-lang","name":"hd-lang","description":"My Toy Language","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-19T04:44:06Z","updated":"2026-10-08T07:24:42Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://herringtondarkholme.github.io/hd-lang/","topics":[],"demo":"https://herringtondarkholme.github.io/hd-lang/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.516Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.516Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.516Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.516Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A statically typed, indentation-based language that compiles to WebAssembly, built for code that AI writes and humans review.","Without requirements, a function that sends mail and reads the clock looks like any other, and a test must patch globals or pull in a mocking library to check it. With them, the signature lists what the function touches, and the test installs a fake mailer and a fixed clock for one block. Forgetting a provider is a missing-requirement compile error, not a runtime surprise.","Typed facts and structural derive generate them in plain hd. No macros, no codegen."],"features":["Serialization, schemas, property tests, and fake data from your types.","Effects you can review. A signature shows every capability a function","Sandboxed. Wasm GC, with host access only through requirements."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HerringtonDarkholme/hd-lang/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"08b1d2966a9b670b06fa5dda50bd90e8cdb82a92e3e418fa2f772ec97d918941","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.697Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.697Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A statically typed, indentation-based language that compiles to WebAssembly, built for code that AI writes and humans review.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HerringtonDarkholme/hd-lang/bl